WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.382
So far, GROUP BY has produced one summary grain at a time.

00:00:04.382 --> 00:00:09.327
Advanced grouping features let one query produce several summary levels.

00:00:09.327 --> 00:00:13.952
GROUPING SETS lets you explicitly list the summary combinations you want.

00:00:13.952 --> 00:00:19.617
ROLLUP is useful for hierarchical reports, such as category, then product, then a grand total.

00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:25.977
CUBE generates every grouping combination of the listed dimensions.

00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:32.442
These features reduce the need to write several separate aggregation queries and combine them manually.

00:00:32.442 --> 00:00:37.157
The tradeoff is that the output contains different grains in the same result.

00:00:37.157 --> 00:00:43.502
That means you must understand what each row represents and how subtotal placeholders are displayed.

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:48.627
We will use a small product-sales table so you can see those levels clearly.

00:00:48.627 --> 00:00:54.137
Connect this idea to a student-success report comparing course-level outcomes.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:59.592
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:07.292
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:12.762
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:01:12.762 --> 00:01:18.480
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
